<!--
    Type campaign, item `ptrfromuse`: a function parameter that the body only
    ever dereferences is declared as an integer.  coreutils fmt -O2 shows the
    split, on two functions that take the same kind of argument:

        void sub_3000(unsigned long *a0)          // dereferenced at offset 0
        void sub_3420(long a0, unsigned int a1)   // dereferenced at +8, +0x10

    Root cause (P5, type propagation).  `ActionInferTypes` seeds every Varnode
    from local op semantics and then pushes the seeds along the def-use graph,
    and neither half can reach the second parameter.  In the seed fold
    (`getLocalType`), every reader of `a0` is an `INT_ADD`, and
    `TypeOpIntAdd::getInputLocal` votes `int8` for each of them, so there is no
    pointer candidate at all.  The pointer that DOES exist (measured with an
    instrumented build, `TypeOp::propagateToPointer` types the `a0 + 8` result
    `undefined8 *` on every pass) never travels back to `a0`, because
    `TypeOpIntAdd::propagateType` (typeop.cc:1217) refuses to carry a pointer
    from an output to an input.  On the same run that refusal fires twelve times
    with `a0` itself as the target.

    Stage / sub-stage: P5 "type-propagation".  The P0 assertion
    `option ptrfromuse off|byte|void` decides whether a use-derived pointer is
    offered as one more vote in that fold, and what it points at.

    The fixture is the same shape on SysV x86-64, plus two controls:

        sumfields:   mov eax,[rdi+8]; add eax,[rdi+0x10]; ret
                     the witness - RDI is only ever a memory base
        scaledbase:  shl rdi,2; mov eax,[rdi+8]; ret
                     a control - RDI is SHIFTED before it is dereferenced, which
                     no pointer survives, so the rule must decline
        derefzero:   mov eax,[rdi]; ret
                     a control - an offset-0 dereference already types the
                     parameter upstream, so nothing here may move it
        globalindex: movsx eax,byte [rdi+0x200000]; ret
                     a control - the same INT_ADD shape with the roles reversed:
                     the constant is a global byte table and RDI is the subscript
                     (`table[i]`).  Typing the subscript would both lie about the
                     parameter and replace the named global with its raw address,
                     so the rule must decline
        blindindex:  movsx eax,byte [rdi+0x300000]; ret
                     a control - the same shape with NOTHING mapped at the
                     constant, which is what a stripped image's .bss table looks
                     like.  Address-like with no symbol settles nothing, so the
                     addition neither carries the walk nor refuses it, and a
                     parameter with no other use is still declined

    Pass 1 (`option ptrfromuse off`) reproduces the bug; pass 2 (`byte`) and
    pass 3 (`void`) are the two shipped pointees.  All three controls are
    identical in all three passes.
-->
